APLAN020: a live task waiting on a `dropped` one can never legitimately start.
The plan is deadlocked, and `check`, the gate, must say so rather than pass.

```
$ aplan check
? 1
error[APLAN020] C-002: is `todo` but blocker `C-001` is `dropped`: it can never legitimately start
  --> aplan/tasks/C-002.md
failed: 1 error(s), 0 warning(s) across 2 tasks

```

`ready` and `why` already knew: a dropped blocker does not satisfy a dependency.

```
$ aplan ready
```

```
$ aplan why C-002
C-002 is blocked by:
  C-001 [dropped]  Abandoned approach

